## What the setup does

| Step | What | Where |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | Detects the system, the proxy, TLS interception, OneDrive and the network | `~/.workshop-claude/ca.pem` (only with a company certificate) |
| 1 | git (Mac: Command Line Tools; Windows: Git for Windows for the current user only) | system / `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Git` |
| 2 | Claude Code {{CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION}} (official installer) | `~/.local/bin` |
| 3 | Console login (`claude auth login --console`) | Keychain / `~/.claude` |
| 4 | Node.js (the existing one if ≥ {{NODE_MIN_MAJOR}}; otherwise {{NODE_VERSION}}, verified with SHA-256) | `~/.workshop-claude/node` |
| 5 | uv {{UV_VERSION}} | `~/.local/bin` |
| 6 | GitHub CLI {{GH_VERSION}} and `gh auth login` | `~/.workshop-claude/bin` |
| 7 | Jira MCP (Atlassian), user scope | `~/.claude.json` |
| 8 | Skills, `ws-*` agents, cost hooks and statusline, with a safe merge of `settings.json` | `~/.claude/`, `~/.workshop-claude/kit` |
| 9 | Workshop projects | `~/workshop-claude/` |
| 10 | Agent Memory app {{MEMORY_APP_VERSION}} (optional, does not block) | `uv tool`, `~/.agent-memory` |
| 11 | Claude Desktop (optional, `{{FLAG_SEM_DESKTOP}}` skips it) | `~/Applications` |
| 12 | Final test with Haiku and the cost from `pricing.json` | — |

Everything installed is recorded in `~/.workshop-claude/manifest.json`. `settings.json` is backed up in `~/.workshop-claude/backup/`. The log (without secrets) is in `~/.workshop-claude/setup.log`.

**Languages.** The setup speaks English only, and so do its options (the old Portuguese ones still work). It detects the machine language and, if you don't have Claude Code's `language` setting yet, writes it (Portuguese, English, Hindi or Hebrew). The skills and agents are written in English and answer in your language. The Arena, the orchestrator and the statusline are in Portuguese on a Portuguese machine and in English on all others. To choose the language yourself, give the setup `WORKSHOP_LANG` with `pt-BR`, `pt-PT`, `en`, `hi` or `he`: on macOS put it after the pipe, right before `bash` (`curl -fsSL {{SETUP_MAC_URL}} | WORKSHOP_LANG=pt-BR bash`; `WORKSHOP_LANG=pt-BR curl …` only reaches `curl`), and on Windows run `$env:WORKSHOP_LANG='pt-BR'` first. The language chosen at install is kept when you run the setup again; only `WORKSHOP_LANG` changes it, and a value the setup doesn't know is ignored, with a note.

## Layout

| Folder | Contents |
|---|---|
| `setup/` | `setup-mac.sh`, `setup-windows.ps1`, `bootstrap-windows.ps1` and the message catalogs: `messages.en.json` (what the setup shows) and `messages.pt.json` (the Portuguese TROUBLESHOOTING) |
| `installer/` | Node installer, the same on both systems (`install-user.mjs`, `assemble-demo.mjs`, `assemble-sandbox.mjs`) |
| `hooks/`, `statusline/`, `orchestrator/` | Cost measurement and swarm orchestration |
| `skills-demo/`, `skills-prod/`, `skills-shared/`, `agents/` | Skills and agents (in English; they answer in the user's language) |
| `demo-project/`, `practice-project/` | Hands-on projects |
| `tools/` | `render.mjs`, `build-release.sh`, `publish-release.sh`, `switch-repos.*`, `check-repo.mjs` and the tests |
| `docs/` | Guides in English: install, troubleshooting, FAQ, publishing, organizer. Portuguese in `docs/pt/`; the install guide also in `docs/hi/` and `docs/he/` |

## For the organizer

- All URLs and versions are in `repos.conf`. This README is generated: edit the templates in `tools/templates/<language>/` (`en`, `pt`, `hi`, `he`) and run `node tools/render.mjs`.
- Release: `tools/build-release.sh {{WORKSHOP_VERSION}}` (creates `dist/{{WORKSHOP_VERSION}}/`) and `tools/publish-release.sh {{WORKSHOP_VERSION}}` (creates the release at {{RELEASE_URL}}).
- Check the repository: `node tools/check-repo.mjs`. Tests: `node --test tools/test/` and `bash setup/test/test-mac.sh`.
- Move to the public repositories: [docs/PUBLISHING.md](docs/PUBLISHING.md).
- Decisions and sources (in Portuguese): [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md).

If you want to verify before running, the SHA-256 checksums are at {{SHA256SUMS_URL}}.
